    "result_text": "The full suite is green. `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and both of its tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `locality` field derived from an owner's city using the fixed city-to-region table.\n\nThe codebase already had a clear pattern for derived read-only owner fields (`displayName`, `initials`, `membershipTier`, etc.): declared in the OpenAPI schema and computed in the MapStruct `OwnerMapper` during DTO mapping. I followed that same idiom:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `locality` read-only property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `toLocality` mapping method backed by a fixed `CITY_REGION` table (`Sydney->NSW`, `Melbourne->VIC`, `Brisbane->QLD`), returning the canonical region or `\"UNKNOWN\"` when the city isn't listed.\n\nBoth acceptance tests (`coreDerivesRegionForKnownCity` \u2192 NSW for Sydney, and `functionalityUnknownCityIsUnknown` \u2192 UNKNOWN for a random city) pass, and the full test suite builds green.",
